          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"cofield-nikkis-touch-a6c228d3d88d554f\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":3,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Franco directly avows his love for Nikki, strongly supporting T. Because the avowal immediately frames a marriage proposal and a shared future, it also helps enact a serious relational undertaking, supporting P. The described emotion intensifies the delivery but does not independently establish reflex-like expressive force, so E receives no support.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The main uncertainty is how much of the commitment force belongs to the love utterance itself rather than to the immediately following marriage proposal; this limits P below the maximum.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Franco directly addresses Nikki during a planned marriage proposal: “I love you more than words could ever express.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The utterance is part of a carefully planned proposal involving a ring, romantic setting, and assembled family. It presents Franco's love as both a current emotional state and a basis for marriage and a shared future. His emotional voice and the heightened scene indicate intensity, but the wording is deliberate and integrated into the proposal rather than portrayed as an involuntary verbal discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"ev1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I love you more than words could ever express.”\",\"supports\":\"A direct and emphatic avowal of Franco's loving emotional state, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“You’ve changed my life... You make me a better man, and I can’t imagine my future without you in it. Will you marry me?”\",\"supports\":\"The avowal is integrated into a proposal and future-oriented relational undertaking, supporting P.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Franco has arranged the trip, restaurant, ring, waiter, and presence of Nikki's family before delivering the utterance.\",\"supports\":\"The speech is planned and deliberative, weighing against interpreting its core force as reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"ev4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration describes Franco's voice as “full of emotion.”\",\"supports\":\"The delivery is emotionally intense, but this alone does not provide independent evidence for E.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the core avowal and its proposal-linked undertaking. Emotional intensity is adequately represented as contextual delivery evidence without adding E, and no important residual core force requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
